  "id": "relief",
  "term": "relief",
  "definition": "Relief is a short-term easing of negative emotion in the moment, such as after a supportive interaction. In this context, it is distinct from adaptive emotion regulation because feeling better right away does not by itself mean a person has strengthened their ability to manage future emotions on their own.",
